<html>
<title>Sound</title>
<body>


<h1>Sound</h1>

<p>
Sound emulation can be adjusted using the controls shown below:
</p>

<p>
<img src="images/computer_sound.png" border="0" width="724" height="609">
</p>
<ul>
<li>(1) <strong>Volume</strong> slider</li>
<li>(2) <strong>Tempo</strong> slider</li>
</ul>

<p>
Sound volume can be changed by dragging the <strong>Volume</strong> slider (1). Sound can be turned off by dragging the slider to the far left.
</p>

<p>
When a COSMAC VIP with a VP550 or VP551 board is configured, the <strong>Tempo</strong> slider (2) is enabled. The VP550/551 tempo can be changed by dragging the slider.
</p>


<h2>Equalization</h2>

<p>
Equalization can be changed by selecting an option from the <strong>Settings/Equalization</strong> menu (1), shown below. By default, <tt>TV Speaker</tt> is selected.
</p>

<p>
<img src="images/computer_sound_equalization.png" border="0" width="439" height="272">
</p>
<ul>
<li>(1) <strong>Equalization</strong> menu item</li>
</ul>
</body>
</html>
